\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Biexponential fit lifetimes with 95\% repeat-scan bootstrap confidence intervals. Each lifetime is written as the fitted value followed by $[\text  {lower bound},\text  {upper bound}]$, in ps. The bounds are the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles of fits obtained by resampling complete retained scans. They quantify repeat-scan variability conditional on the selected scans and model; model uncertainty is excluded. The filename value is the phase-mask period; the sample period is one quarter of that value. Supplied delay coordinates, periods, and derived wave numbers are treated as exact.}}{19}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
