\newlabel{fig:rate-q2}{{11}{23}{Slow-component rates against $q^2$: horizontal coordinates are calculated from the filename periods and the email's factor-of-four demagnification, while vertical coordinates are inverse slow lifetimes fitted to the recorded traces. Supplied delays and grating spacings are treated as exact. The finite-$q$ line gives the TG-only diffusion estimate; including the $q=0$ PP rate gives a poor linear fit. Bars show conditional 95\% repeat-scan intervals for the rates; the dotted line shows the borderline-scan sensitivity}{figure.11}{}}
