\newlabel{fig:iac-residuals}{{12}{27}{Selected autocorrelation fit residuals, normalized by the measured range in the fitted interval. Structured residuals remain after nonlinear fringe calibration and indicate that covariance errors alone understate uncertainty. RMS diagnostic uncertainties are unestimated; $\chi ^2_\nu $ is unavailable without pointwise measurement errors (Appendix~\ref {app:chi-squared})}{figure.12}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Recorded fringe rate: blue points are inverse separations between successive measured maxima, placed at interval midpoints; red curves give the fitted delay-map derivative and dashed lines the central rate. Wider fringe spacing toward the edges supports a nonuniform delay scan. This is a recorded fringe rate, distinct from the optical carrier frequency. Pointwise uncertainties are unquantified; peak selection is explained in Sec.~\ref {sec:iac-derivation}.}}{28}{figure.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fringe-calibration}{{13}{28}{Recorded fringe rate: blue points are inverse separations between successive measured maxima, placed at interval midpoints; red curves give the fitted delay-map derivative and dashed lines the central rate. Wider fringe spacing toward the edges supports a nonuniform delay scan. This is a recorded fringe rate, distinct from the optical carrier frequency. Pointwise uncertainties are unquantified; peak selection is explained in Sec.~\ref {sec:iac-derivation}}{figure.13}{}}
